From: Christian Marangi <ansuelsmth@gmail.com>

Allow DSA to move a user port between the local QCA8K CPU ports or
onto a LAG made from those ports. Update both sides of lookup
membership so traffic can flow only between the user port and its
selected conduit.

A CPU port can join or leave a conduit LAG without DSA changing the
conduit netdev of user ports already assigned to that LAG. Wrap the
LAG callbacks and refresh those users after hardware trunk membership
changes. Derive bridge membership from the complete conduit mask as
well, so a later bridge rejoin does not reduce a conduit LAG to one
physical CPU port.

Snapshot both directions of the old lookup membership before a live
change and restore them if any register update fails. This keeps the
hardware on the old conduit when DSA rejects or unwinds the change.

